# [P2] Lemma A.69 (m = 2, n = 3): a plain green dot (1 -> 2) of dimension mn, each output into a
# splitter, the first with a plain green effect on its n output and the second on its m output, is
# the splitter.
# Dimensions are literal. Paper pink spiders are X spiders with their normalisation d^((m+n)/2 - 1) as scalar.
# A mixed-dimensional Z box is its definition ([P2] (2.3.3)): a Z box over the product of its leg
# dimensions, each leg through a binder or splitter whose other leg carries a pink dot.

@lhs =
    z1 = Z(1 -> 2, literal 6)
    s2 = S(literal 2, literal 3)
    s3 = S(literal 2, literal 3)
    z4 = Z(1 -> 0, literal 3)
    z5 = Z(1 -> 0, literal 2)
    wire z1.out0 -- s2.in0, z1.out1 -- s3.in0, s2.out1 -- z4.in0, s3.out0 -- z5.in0
    inputs z1.in0
    outputs s2.out0, s3.out1

@rhs =
    s1 = S(literal 2, literal 3)
    inputs s1.in0
    outputs s1.out0, s1.out1

load @lhs
prove against @rhs
certificate kernel
